## Why This Is Asked

Data provenance in multi-tenant analytics platforms is critical for compliance, cross-tenant data sharing, and debugging lineage issues. This question evaluates the ability to integrate Azure data cataloging services, OpenAI-powered analysis, and per-tenant security controls into a production-grade pipeline.

## Key Concepts

- Data provenance and lineage tracking
- Microsoft Purview for metadata management
- Cognitive Search-powered versioned knowledge base
- Role-based access control (RBAC) with Azure Active Directory
- Data Lake auditing and logging
- Drift detection in ingestion pipelines

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lineage consistency validation
const validateLineage = (event) => {
  return event.source && event.sink && event.transactionId;
};

// Drift detection logic
const detectDrift = (expected, actual) => {
  return expected.source !== actual.source || 
         expected.sink !== actual.sink;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle real-time vs. batch lineage processing?
- What strategies would you use to minimize AI hallucinations when assessing lineage accuracy?
- How would you design the RBAC model to support nested tenant hierarchies?

## Why This Is Asked

